## WORKFLOW & RELEASE RULES
- Restart Cursor completely after making configuration changes.  Use `killall Cursor && open -a Cursor` (macOS) or the equivalent for your operating system.  **User confirmation required before using `killall` command.**
- Install MCP servers using `npm install -g @modelcontextprotocol/server-github @modelcontextprotocol/server-git @modelcontextprotocol/server-gitlab`
- Use `npm install -g @modelcontextprotocol/server-github@latest` to update the GitHub MCP server. Update other MCP servers as needed using `npm install -g @modelcontextprotocol/server-git@latest` and `npm install -g @modelcontextprotocol/server-gitlab@latest`.


## REFERENCE EXAMPLES
- To create a new file:  ```Create a new file called test.md in my current repository```
- To list open issues: ```List the open issues in the modelcontextprotocol/servers repository```
- To create a new file and add content using MCP: ```Create a new file called test-mcp.md in the current repository with the content "Testing MCP integration"```
- To verify MCP integration, create a file and commit/push using the following commands:
 ```bash
git add test-mcp.md
git commit -m "test: Add MCP integration test file"
git push origin main
```
- To check GitHub remote configuration:
```bash
git remote -v | cat
```
- To determine the latest Cursor version location, perform a search across all project directories.  Also check the two MCP configuration locations detailed in PROJECT DOCUMENTATION & CONTEXT SYSTEM.


