## DEBUGGING
- To enable debug logging in Cursor, add these settings to `cursor/settings.json`:
 ```json
 {
  "cursor.experimental.anthropic.claude.debug": true,
  "cursor.experimental.anthropic.claude.logLevel": "debug"
 }
 ```
- Check Cursor's Developer Tools (Cmd+Option+I on Mac, Ctrl+Shift+I on Windows/Linux) for MCP-related logs in the Console tab.  If the logs directory does not exist, ensure the MCP servers are properly installed.
- To 100% verify MCP usage, examine Cursor's debug logs for MCP-related activity after enabling debug logging.  The logs will show the commands executed via MCP.  Use `cat ~/Library/Application\ Support/Cursor/User/logs/main.log | grep -i mcp | tail -50` to view the last 50 lines of MCP-related logs.
- The error `spawn npx ENOENT` indicates that the `npx` command couldn't be found. Use  `/opt/homebrew/opt/node@20/bin/npx` or equivalent path if `npx` is not globally available.  Use `node -e "require('@modelcontextprotocol/server-github')" ` style configuration for each server.  Error -32000 indicates connection issues; check network connectivity and permissions.  "Failed to create client" error using the direct `node` method may require further investigation.


## FINAL DOs AND DON'Ts
- Ensure your GitHub token has the necessary permissions (`repo` and `read:org` scopes).  Also ensure your GitLab token has the necessary permissions.
- Restart Cursor completely after making configuration changes. Use `killall Cursor && open -a Cursor` (macOS) or the equivalent for your operating system. **User confirmation required before using `killall` command.**
- Regularly update the MCP server: `npm install -g @modelcontextprotocol/server-github@latest`  Also update other MCP servers as needed using `npm install -g @modelcontextprotocol/server-git@latest` and `npm install -g @modelcontextprotocol/server-gitlab@latest`.
- Verify MCP integration by checking Cursor's debug logs for MCP-related activity.
- When unsure of the latest Cursor version location, conduct a thorough search across all project directories and check the MCP configuration files.
- For GitLab MCP server setup, generate a personal access token from GitLab (User Settings > Access Tokens) and replace `"YOUR_GITLAB_TOKEN_HERE"` with your token in the `~/.cursor/mcp.json` file.  The preferred location for user-specific MCP configurations is `~/.cursor/mcp.json`.
- To install MCP servers reliably, use `npm install -g @modelcontextprotocol/server-github @modelcontextprotocol/server-git @modelcontextprotocol/server-gitlab`.  Consider using the `node -e "require('@modelcontextprotocol/server-github')" ` style configuration for each server for improved reliability.  Ensure that the `python` command is available in the system's PATH.  If using Anaconda, create a symbolic link using `ln -s $(which python3) ~/.local/bin/python`.